OL,3,C'Justice is served': Survivor speaks
OL,4,Cout as abuser jailed 35 years later
OL,6,FNow 59, Singh showed no emotion as the
OL,7,Fwoman read aloud her victim impact
OL,8,Fstatement in court, detailing the long-
OL,9,Fterm impact his actions still have on
OL,10,Fher everyday life.
OL,12,FSentencing him, the Judge said: "I
OL,13,Fhope when you are serving your
OL,14,Fsentence you work on accepting what
OL,15,Fyou have done and the effect it has
OL,16,Fhad."
OL,18,FReflecting on the sentence, the woman
OL,19,Fspoke candidly about the ongoing anger
OL,20,Fshe carries: "Angry, I'm still angry.
OL,21,FI have to carry this, why can't you?"
OL,1,W~k4j5 hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}      G3/6
OL,2,W/*%+.-' "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,
